# Purpose: Preserve externally supplied text byte-for-byte in a named archive copy without interpreting shell-looking content.
# Inputs: intake/clipboard-capture.txt: externally supplied plain text.
# Outputs: archive/intake/clipboard-capture.txt: literal archived copy; stdout echoes the saved text.
accept clipboard_capture_path as text with default "intake/clipboard-capture.txt"
run mkdir with flags ["-p"] and paths ["archive/intake"]
run cat with path clipboard_capture_path
then save to "archive/intake/clipboard-capture.txt"
